<Base title="About" description="Why ELI10 Cyber exists: a commercial leader from ad tech learning cybersecurity in public.">
  <article class="wrap prose measure">
    <h1>Hi, I’m Vas.</h1>
    <p>I’ve spent over seven years in digital advertising. I’ve been on the buy side at EssenceMediaCom (GroupM), on the sell side at Sportradar where I led an inside sales team, and before that I led a sales team on the Meta project for small and medium businesses.</p>
    <p>Now I’m moving into cybersecurity. I’m studying for CompTIA Security+ (SY0-701), and I’ve found that the best way to really understand something like a protocol is to explain it as if to a ten-year-old, then draw it.</p>
    <p>This site is where those explanations live. It’s for anyone who is switching into security mid-career, especially from sales, marketing, account management or other commercial roles, and wants to understand the technology well enough to have real conversations with engineers and buyers.</p>

    <h2>What makes it different</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Simple first, correct second.</strong> Every lesson starts with a picture and a story, then gives you the proper terms.</li>
      <li><strong>The buyer’s view.</strong> Each lesson ends with why a company would care and spend money on it. That’s the part commercial people need most and courses rarely cover.</li>
      <li><strong>Built with AI, checked by a human.</strong> I draft with AI tools and fact-check against official documentation. If you spot a mistake, tell me and I’ll fix it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Say hello</h2>
    <p>The best place to follow along is <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/vevangelopoulos" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">LinkedIn</a>, where I post each new lesson. You can also email <a href="mailto:hello@eli10cyber.com">hello@eli10cyber.com</a>.</p>
  </article>
